1
00:00:15,439 --> 00:00:19,330
Listen to me! Be calm!

2
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:23,287
Please be quiet! Thank you.

3
00:00:29,839 --> 00:00:32,649
Let's be quiet. Let's be calm.

4
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:35,001
Please don't shout and scream.

5
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:38,362
Let's go quickly. Let's start now.

6
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:40,841
Let's get Amanda back.

7
00:00:41,359 --> 00:00:44,329
<i>Corvax! Thimbo! What</i> a <i>pair!</i>

8
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:46,881
Where's Amanda now?

9
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:49,965
Let's go carefully. Let's go quietly.

10
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:52,281
Let's get Amanda back.

11
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:55,205
Let's get Amanda back.

12
00:00:55,399 --> 00:00:57,720
Let's get Amanda back.

13
00:00:57,920 --> 00:01:00,126
Look! Look, your Majesty!

14
00:01:00,399 --> 00:01:03,641
-This was near the river. -Corvax!

15
00:01:03,840 --> 00:01:05,523
Quick! Let's go to the river.

16
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:12,210
The King's boat isn't here.

17
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:14,049
Corvax has got it.

18
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:17,961
Let's take one of these boats. Let's take this one.

19
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:21,728
That's an old boat, Muzzy.

20
00:01:21,920 --> 00:01:25,082
It's all right. Let's take it. We can catch them.

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,205
Corvax?

22
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:34,130
-Yes? -Where are we going?

23
00:01:34,519 --> 00:01:37,921
Ah! That's a secret.

24
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:41,681
Come on, Corvax! Tell me!

25
00:01:41,879 --> 00:01:43,687
No! It's a secret.

26
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:48,087
Corvax, why are we taking the baby?

27
00:01:48,680 --> 00:01:52,764
Because she can help us.

28
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:56,362
She can't help us. She can't talk.

29
00:01:56,599 --> 00:01:58,920
She can't talk now.

30
00:02:00,359 --> 00:02:02,202
But I can teach her.

31
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:03,765
Then she can talk.

32
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:07,846
I can teach her... everything.

33
00:02:08,919 --> 00:02:11,729
She can learn everything from me.

34
00:02:12,159 --> 00:02:14,526
She's Sylvia's daughter.

35
00:02:14,719 --> 00:02:18,166
I want to marry her. I want to be the King!

36
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:20,767
The King of Gondoland!

37
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:24,884
And Amanda my Queen!

38
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,570
Don't do that!

39
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,810
Bob, what's that over there?

40
00:02:38,159 --> 00:02:40,684
-Where? -Look! On the right.

41
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:42,491
Near that big tree.

42
00:02:43,719 --> 00:02:45,483
I can't see anything.

43
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:48,800
There is something over there, Bob.

44
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:50,525
No, there isn't.

45
00:02:50,960 --> 00:02:52,484
There isn't anything.

46
00:02:53,319 --> 00:02:55,208
I can hear something.

47
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:57,404
Can you hear it?

48
00:02:59,199 --> 00:03:00,848
That's a bird.

49
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:04,125
Muzzy, can you see anything?

50
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:11,686
There's something in this box.

51
00:03:12,039 --> 00:03:14,689
There isn't anything in this one.

52
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:18,090
Is there anything in that box?

53
00:03:19,120 --> 00:03:21,487
There was something in it,

54
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:23,648
but there isn't anything now.

55
00:03:24,159 --> 00:03:26,048
There's nothing in it.

56
00:03:26,360 --> 00:03:28,488
Look! Nothing!

57
00:03:28,919 --> 00:03:29,919
Oh dear!

58
00:03:45,080 --> 00:03:47,401
I'm hungry.

59
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,001
-Have you got any... -Clocks?

60
00:03:50,199 --> 00:03:52,804
No, we haven't got anything for you, Muzzy.

61
00:03:53,039 --> 00:03:54,609
No clocks?

62
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:57,006
No. No clocks.

63
00:03:57,199 --> 00:03:58,199
Nothing.

64
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,240
Careful, Muzzy!

65
00:04:01,439 --> 00:04:04,044
Go right! No! Right!

66
00:04:04,319 --> 00:04:07,084
-What's the matter. -You're going left.

67
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:08,566
Go right!

68
00:04:09,879 --> 00:04:11,449
That's better.

69
00:04:11,680 --> 00:04:13,250
Now go straight on.

70
00:04:21,639 --> 00:04:24,289
<i>Go left, go left, go left...</i>

71
00:04:27,399 --> 00:04:30,084
Go right, go right, go right.

72
00:04:32,879 --> 00:04:35,802
Go straight on... Go straight on...

73
00:04:36,600 --> 00:04:38,283
Yes! Straight on.

74
00:04:43,560 --> 00:04:46,085
You can be the King, Corvax.

75
00:04:46,279 --> 00:04:47,962
But what about me?

76
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:51,926
Oh, you can be important, Thimbo.

77
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:54,050
Important?

78
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:56,607
Yes. Important.

79
00:04:58,160 --> 00:05:00,560
Once upon a time...

80
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:07,247
Once upon a time, I was important.

81
00:05:07,720 --> 00:05:10,041
Very important.

82
00:05:10,560 --> 00:05:13,802
-Where you? -Yes, I was.

83
00:05:14,759 --> 00:05:16,807
Was Bob important?

84
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,968
No, he wasn't.

85
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:26,364
Bob wasn't important. He was the... gardener.

86
00:05:26,720 --> 00:05:30,007
I said 'Count the flowers!'

87
00:05:32,120 --> 00:05:33,610
What happened?

88
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:35,723
He counted the flowers.

89
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,241
But then...

90
00:05:41,160 --> 00:05:44,322
What happened then? Tell me, Corvax.

91
00:05:45,480 --> 00:05:48,689
He went away with Princess Sylvia.

92
00:05:49,680 --> 00:05:52,080
They went away on his motorbike.

93
00:05:52,759 --> 00:05:54,648
Did they go far?

94
00:05:54,839 --> 00:05:56,920
No, they didn't.

95
00:05:57,600 --> 00:05:59,408
They didn't go far.

96
00:05:59,959 --> 00:06:01,529
Did you catch them?

97
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:04,168
Yes, I did.

98
00:06:05,279 --> 00:06:07,202
They took Bob away.

99
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:09,403
They put him in prison.

100
00:06:09,759 --> 00:06:11,1000
But Muzzy was there.

101
00:06:12,639 --> 00:06:14,163
They got out.

102
00:06:16,959 --> 00:06:19,484
What about Princess Sylvia?

103
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:20,966
Did you love her?

104
00:06:21,240 --> 00:06:23,811
Yes, I did.

105
00:06:24,079 --> 00:06:25,843
I loved Sylvia.

106
00:06:26,040 --> 00:06:27,848
I wanted to marry her.

107
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:30,967
But the computer...

108
00:06:32,199 --> 00:06:36,090
the computer! Oh, it was terrible!

109
00:06:36,319 --> 00:06:37,843
Tell me, Corvax.

110
00:06:38,160 --> 00:06:39,446
What did you do?

111
00:06:40,839 --> 00:06:42,647
I didn't do anything.

112
00:06:43,040 --> 00:06:45,008
It was the computer.

113
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:48,246
There were lots of Sylvias.

114
00:06:48,839 --> 00:06:50,728
Did you make them?

115
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:55,442
No, I didn't make them. The computer made them.

116
00:06:56,879 --> 00:06:59,962
Lots of Sylvias!

117
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:02,769
Did they love you?

118
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:05,527
No, they didn't.

119
00:07:06,120 --> 00:07:08,326
They hated me.

120
00:07:10,879 --> 00:07:12,369
Tell me.

121
00:07:12,959 --> 00:07:15,007
Were you here this morning?

122
00:07:16,079 --> 00:07:17,728
Yes, we were.

123
00:07:18,759 --> 00:07:20,840
Did you see anything?

124
00:07:21,439 --> 00:07:23,282
No, I didn't.

125
00:07:23,759 --> 00:07:25,727
Did you hear anything?

126
00:07:26,319 --> 00:07:28,208
Yes, we did.

127
00:07:29,040 --> 00:07:31,008
What did you hear?

128
00:07:32,079 --> 00:07:34,446
We heard a funny noise.

129
00:07:46,360 --> 00:07:48,249
What's the baby doing?

130
00:07:48,560 --> 00:07:50,766
She's pulling the plug out.

131
00:07:50,959 --> 00:07:53,326
She's pulling the plug out!

132
00:07:54,759 --> 00:07:56,840
The water's coming in!

133
00:07:57,040 --> 00:07:58,564
The boat's sinking.

134
00:07:58,759 --> 00:08:01,763
Quick! Take the baby and her things!

135
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:07,400
Thimbo! Help!

136
00:08:09,279 --> 00:08:11,122
I can't swim.

137
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:27,085
It's all right now. You can walk here.

138
00:08:27,319 --> 00:08:28,649
It isn't deep.

139
00:08:34,919 --> 00:08:36,364
That's better!

140
00:08:39,559 --> 00:08:41,560
Did you get the things from the boat?

141
00:08:41,759 --> 00:08:43,760
Yes, I did. They're here.

142
00:08:44,320 --> 00:08:45,366
Well!

143
00:08:45,639 --> 00:08:48,289
Well, the baby's happy.

144
00:08:48,879 --> 00:08:52,166
She's dry. She didn't get wet.

145
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:54,124
No, she didn't.

146
00:08:54,639 --> 00:08:56,447
Did you get wet, Corvax?

147
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:00,924
Yes, I did! Of course I got wet.

148
00:09:01,639 --> 00:09:04,722
What did you do, naughty baby?

149
00:09:04,919 --> 00:09:07,047
You pulled the plug out.

150
00:09:07,519 --> 00:09:09,680
And what happened then?

151
00:09:09,919 --> 00:09:11,1000
The water came in.

152
00:09:12,799 --> 00:09:15,166
And what did the boat do?

153
00:09:15,519 --> 00:09:17,248
The boat sank.

154
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:20,080
Oh shut up!

155
00:09:20,879 --> 00:09:23,564
Come on! You carry the baby.

156
00:09:24,159 --> 00:09:25,683
What about these things?

157
00:09:25,879 --> 00:09:28,359
Oh, you can carry them, too.

158
00:09:30,120 --> 00:09:33,249
Hey, Corvax! You carry something!

159
00:09:33,559 --> 00:09:35,402
Now, Thimbo! Don't be silly!

160
00:09:35,639 --> 00:09:37,562
I'm important.

161
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:40,283
Let's go that way.

162
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:44,279
-Which way, Corvax? -That way, stupid!

163
00:09:51,519 --> 00:09:52,805
Look, Bob!

164
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:55,525
-What's that over there? -Where?

165
00:09:55,759 --> 00:09:57,567
Over there!

166
00:09:58,159 --> 00:10:00,320
It looks like a boat.

167
00:10:00,919 --> 00:10:03,047
It is a boat.

168
00:10:03,759 --> 00:10:06,159
-Go that way, Muzzy. -This way?

169
00:10:06,360 --> 00:10:07,565
No. That's wrong!

170
00:10:07,799 --> 00:10:09,085
Go the other way.

171
00:10:09,320 --> 00:10:12,163
Oh, look! That's their boat.

172
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:14,443
Is there anyone in it?

173
00:10:16,679 --> 00:10:18,760
No, I can't see anyone.

174
00:10:19,480 --> 00:10:21,244
There's no one in it.

175
00:10:21,679 --> 00:10:22,725
Don't worry.

176
00:10:23,360 --> 00:10:25,328
Let's look over there.

177
00:10:33,799 --> 00:10:36,040
Which way did they go?

178
00:10:41,080 --> 00:10:43,321
Did they go this way?

179
00:10:43,519 --> 00:10:45,408
Did they? Did they?

180
00:10:45,600 --> 00:10:47,921
This way? This way?

181
00:10:48,120 --> 00:10:49,928
Did they go this way?

182
00:10:51,200 --> 00:10:53,486
No, they didn't.

183
00:10:53,720 --> 00:10:54,720
No.

184
00:10:55,039 --> 00:10:57,087
Did they go that way?

185
00:10:57,279 --> 00:10:59,247
Did they? Did they?

186
00:10:59,440 --> 00:11:02,045
Perhaps they went that way.

187
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:04,241
That way, that way.

188
00:11:05,480 --> 00:11:07,448
Yes, they did. They did.

189
00:11:07,879 --> 00:11:12,361
Thimbo went that way. That way, that way.

190
00:11:12,559 --> 00:11:17,007
<i>Corvax went that way. That way, that way.</i>

191
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:21,727
Amanda went that way. That way, that way.

192
00:11:22,039 --> 00:11:24,200
Let's go that way, too!

193
00:11:26,080 --> 00:11:28,845
-Come on, Muzzy! -Are you all right, Muzzy?

194
00:11:29,240 --> 00:11:30,320
No.

195
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:33,803
I'm very hungry.

196
00:11:34,120 --> 00:11:37,124
Well, we can't stop now. Come on!

